1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,150
Welcome to Num-Num Numbers. Today, we are counting Lucas numbers inside a sunny clock tower.

2
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:11,715
Our special number wheel remembers two numbers. When they come together, a new number appears.

3
00:00:12,215 --> 00:00:16,889
Look at the rule. Each new Lucas number is the sum of the two numbers just before it.

4
00:00:17,389 --> 00:00:22,650
We choose two starting numbers first. Then we will use the same adding rule, again and again.

5
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:25,136
two

6
00:00:25,936 --> 00:00:31,688
This is our first starting number. Its label is L zero. The small zero is a position label.

7
00:00:33,688 --> 00:00:34,134
one

8
00:00:34,934 --> 00:00:40,832
Our second starting number is smaller than the first. That is right: this sequence starts with two, then one.

9
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:45,750
Both starting numbers stay visible. They are ready to make our first new number together.

10
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:49,061
two plus one equals

11
00:00:49,221 --> 00:00:49,749
three

12
00:00:50,549 --> 00:00:57,462
Two filled counters and one outlined counter have joined. There are three counters altogether. None have disappeared.

13
00:00:57,962 --> 00:01:02,859
Now keep the newer input and the new result. They become the two inputs for the next step.

14
00:01:04,859 --> 00:01:06,197
one plus three equals

15
00:01:06,357 --> 00:01:06,866
four

16
00:01:08,866 --> 00:01:10,202
three plus four equals

17
00:01:10,362 --> 00:01:10,883
seven

18
00:01:12,883 --> 00:01:14,314
four plus seven equals

19
00:01:14,474 --> 00:01:15,043
eleven

20
00:01:15,843 --> 00:01:22,321
Our answer needs two digits now. Four and seven make eleven. Watch one group of ten move to the tens place.

21
00:01:22,821 --> 00:01:28,755
From here, the round labels show number values. A single label can stand for a number much bigger than one.

22
00:01:30,755 --> 00:01:32,350
seven plus eleven equals

23
00:01:32,510 --> 00:01:33,131
eighteen

24
00:01:35,131 --> 00:01:36,733
eleven plus eighteen equals

25
00:01:36,893 --> 00:01:37,639
twenty-nine

26
00:01:39,639 --> 00:01:41,489
eighteen plus twenty-nine equals

27
00:01:41,649 --> 00:01:42,473
forty-seven

28
00:01:44,473 --> 00:01:46,547
twenty-nine plus forty-seven equals

29
00:01:46,707 --> 00:01:47,531
seventy-six

30
00:01:49,531 --> 00:01:51,785
forty-seven plus seventy-six equals

31
00:01:51,945 --> 00:01:53,270
one hundred twenty-three

32
00:01:54,070 --> 00:02:01,056
Let us replay that addition by place. Seven ones plus six ones make thirteen ones. Keep three and carry one ten.

33
00:02:01,556 --> 00:02:07,798
Four tens, seven tens, and the carried ten make twelve tens. Keep two tens and carry one hundred.

34
00:02:08,298 --> 00:02:14,975
One hundred, two tens, and three ones make our result. The replay has not added another term to our sequence.

35
00:02:16,975 --> 00:02:19,626
seventy-six plus one hundred twenty-three equals

36
00:02:19,786 --> 00:02:21,211
one hundred ninety-nine

37
