one hundred ninety-nine plus three hundred twenty-two equals

40
00:02:33,769 --> 00:02:35,070
five hundred twenty-one

41
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:40,497
three hundred twenty-two plus five hundred twenty-one equals

42
00:02:40,657 --> 00:02:41,923
eight hundred forty-three

43
00:02:43,923 --> 00:02:47,484
five hundred twenty-one plus eight hundred forty-three equals

44
00:02:47,644 --> 00:02:49,584
one thousand three hundred sixty-four

45
00:02:51,584 --> 00:02:55,736
eight hundred forty-three plus one thousand three hundred sixty-four equals

46
00:02:55,896 --> 00:02:57,446
two thousand two hundred seven

47
00:02:59,446 --> 00:03:03,949
one thousand three hundred sixty-four plus two thousand two hundred seven equals

48
00:03:04,109 --> 00:03:06,315
three thousand five hundred seventy-one

49
00:03:08,315 --> 00:03:12,952
two thousand two hundred seven plus three thousand five hundred seventy-one equals

50
00:03:13,112 --> 00:03:15,280
five thousand seven hundred seventy-eight

51
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:22,667
three thousand five hundred seventy-one plus five thousand seven hundred seventy-eight equals

52
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:24,841
nine thousand three hundred forty-nine

53
00:03:26,841 --> 00:03:32,148
five thousand seven hundred seventy-eight plus nine thousand three hundred forty-nine equals

54
00:03:32,308 --> 00:03:34,543
fifteen thousand one hundred twenty-seven

55
00:03:35,343 --> 00:03:41,949
The numbers are longer, but the rule stays the same. Two remembered values come in, and one new sum comes out.

56
00:03:42,449 --> 00:03:48,486
Follow the curved arrows. The newest two values move forward, while the older value stays in our history.

57
00:03:50,486 --> 00:03:55,833
nine thousand three hundred forty-nine plus fifteen thousand one hundred twenty-seven equals

58
00:03:55,993 --> 00:03:58,484
twenty-four thousand four hundred seventy-six

59
00:04:00,484 --> 00:04:06,154
fifteen thousand one hundred twenty-seven plus twenty-four thousand four hundred seventy-six equals

60
00:04:06,314 --> 00:04:08,299
thirty-nine thousand six hundred three

61
00:04:10,299 --> 00:04:15,894
twenty-four thousand four hundred seventy-six plus thirty-nine thousand six hundred three equals

62
00:04:16,054 --> 00:04:17,890
sixty-four thousand seventy-nine

63
00:04:19,890 --> 00:04:24,847
thirty-nine thousand six hundred three plus sixty-four thousand seventy-nine equals

64
00:04:25,007 --> 00:04:27,506
one hundred three thousand six hundred eighty-two

65
00:04:29,506 --> 00:04:35,109
sixty-four thousand seventy-nine plus one hundred three thousand six hundred eighty-two equals

66
00:04:35,269 --> 00:04:38,509
one hundred sixty-seven thousand seven hundred sixty-one

67
00:04:40,509 --> 00:04:47,518
one hundred three thousand six hundred eighty-two plus one hundred sixty-seven thousand seven hundred sixty-one equals

68
00:04:47,678 --> 00:04:50,695
two hundred seventy-one thousand four hundred forty-three

69
00:04:52,695 --> 00:05:00,157
one hundred sixty-seven thousand seven hundred sixty-one plus two hundred seventy-one thousand four hundred forty-three equals

70
00:05:00,317 --> 00:05:03,188
four hundred thirty-nine thousand two hundred four

71
00:05:05,188 --> 00:05:12,028
two hundred seventy-one thousand four hundred forty-three plus four hundred thirty-nine thousand two hundred four equals

72
00:05:12,188 --> 00:05:15,229
seven hundred ten thousand six hundred forty-seven

73
00:05:17,229 --> 00:05:23,820
four hundred thirty-nine thousand two hundred four plus seven hundred ten thousand six hundred forty-seven equals

74
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:27,573
one million one hundred forty-nine thousand eight hundred fifty-one

75
00:05:28,373 --> 00:05:33,610
We have passed one million. The commas help us read long numbers in groups of three digits.

76
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:40,794
The round windows will stay wide enough for every digit. Watch the values travel without changing along the way.

77
00:05:42,794 --> 00:05:50,660
