87
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:58,307
seven million eight hundred eighty-one thousand one hundred ninety-six plus twelve million seven hundred fifty-two thousand forty-three equals

88
00:06:58,467 --> 00:07:02,236
twenty million six hundred thirty-three thousand two hundred thirty-nine

89
00:07:04,236 --> 00:07:12,634
twelve million seven hundred fifty-two thousand forty-three plus twenty million six hundred thirty-three thousand two hundred thirty-nine equals

90
00:07:12,794 --> 00:07:16,734
thirty-three million three hundred eighty-five thousand two hundred eighty-two

91
00:07:18,734 --> 00:07:27,807
twenty million six hundred thirty-three thousand two hundred thirty-nine plus thirty-three million three hundred eighty-five thousand two hundred eighty-two equals

92
00:07:27,967 --> 00:07:31,158
fifty-four million eighteen thousand five hundred twenty-one

93
00:07:33,158 --> 00:07:41,582
thirty-three million three hundred eighty-five thousand two hundred eighty-two plus fifty-four million eighteen thousand five hundred twenty-one equals

94
00:07:41,742 --> 00:07:45,094
eighty-seven million four hundred three thousand eight hundred three

95
00:07:45,894 --> 00:07:51,502
Here are the two latest values for the next addition. The result is still hidden until we add them.

96
00:07:53,502 --> 00:08:01,480
fifty-four million eighteen thousand five hundred twenty-one plus eighty-seven million four hundred three thousand eight hundred three equals

97
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:06,438
one hundred forty-one million four hundred twenty-two thousand three hundred twenty-four

98
00:08:07,238 --> 00:08:12,282
This is our first Lucas number above one hundred million. We have one more addition to make.

99
00:08:14,282 --> 00:08:23,642
eighty-seven million four hundred three thousand eight hundred three plus one hundred forty-one million four hundred twenty-two thousand three hundred twenty-four equals

100
00:08:23,802 --> 00:08:28,783
two hundred twenty-eight million eight hundred twenty-six thousand one hundred twenty-seven

101
00:08:30,783 --> 00:08:36,446
We counted forty-one terms, starting with our two chosen values and making thirty-nine new sums.

102
00:08:36,946 --> 00:08:43,375
Two, then one: those starting values made this Lucas sequence. Keep the latest two, add them, and continue.

103
00:08:43,875 --> 00:08:52,884
The same adding rule can begin with different starting values. Fibonacci numbers begin with zero and one; Lucas numbers begin with two and one.

104
00:08:53,384 --> 00:08:58,305
Thank you for counting with us. Our number wheel can keep going, even after we say goodbye.
